#version 450

// vulkan/shaders/noop.comp - the one shader this port builds in Phase 1, and what it is for.
//
// It exists so that the SPIR-V path has a body to be built from: vulkan/CMakeLists.txt runs glslc over this file into
// build-vulkan/spv/noop.spv and tools/embed_spv.py over that into generated/vulkan_shaders/noop.h, which
// vulkan/src/gpu/runtime.cpp feeds to vkCreateShaderModule and vkCreateComputePipelines for each Arc it opened.  That
// is the whole pipeline Phase 2 will run engine kernels through, checked on the real card before any engine kernel
// exists (the engine's entry points are still the 281 generated stubs in vulkan/src/engine/stubs.cpp).
//
// Read the body: there is no loop, no counter, no `while`, no atomic, and no buffer this shader re-reads waiting for
// the host to change it.  That is deliberate, not laziness.  Phase 0 P5 (bench/results/vulkan-caps-2026-10-17.md,
// "P5 host doorbell") measured on this driver that a `coherent volatile` flag written by the host was NEVER observed
// by a dispatch already running - not in HOST_VISIBLE, not in HOST_COHERENT, not in a device-local host-visible type,
// not with the write done before or after the submit.  A shader that polls a host-written flag is therefore not a
// mechanism this port may use, and the two mechanisms it uses instead - a submit to make host work visible to the GPU
// (strata::gpu::nudge_submit) and a timeline semaphore value to make GPU progress visible to the host
// (strata::gpu::wait_timeline) - are both in vulkan/src/gpu/runtime.cpp.  The instrument that measured P5 is
// vulkan/probe/shaders/spin.comp, and it stays in the probe: it is a measurement, not something this runtime dispatches.
//
// Nothing in Phase 1 dispatches this shader.  Building the pipeline is the test; the dispatch of it is not needed for
// that, and no engine work is faked by it.
#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic : require

layout(local_size_x = 1, local_size_y = 1, local_size_z = 1) in;

// The parameter block a CUDA launch's arguments become (runtime.cpp: push constants up to
// maxPushConstantsSize, which the self-check measures as 256 B on both Arcs).
layout(push_constant) uniform Push {
    uint tag;
    uint lane_mask;
} pc;

// One storage binding: the shape every device-address argument of an engine kernel becomes (runtime.cpp's
// record_dispatch writes one VkDescriptorBufferInfo per uint64 in the parameter block, offset from that span, range
// clamped to min(maxStorageBufferRange, maxBufferSize, maxMemoryAllocationSize)).
layout(set = 0, binding = 0) buffer Sink {
    uint value[];
} sink;

void main() {
    // A single write, derived from the push constants and this invocation's subgroup lane.  It proves a dispatch can
    // read its parameter block and write its storage buffer on this driver; it is not a kernel, and it is never run.
    sink.value[0] = pc.tag ^ (gl_SubgroupSize * 65536u + pc.lane_mask);
}
